(2. Describe the process of reporting a lost mobile phone.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
70.8661417322834666 768.1892125984252289 Td
(First, the owner calls the lost number to check whether someone answers or the phone is only misplaced.) Tj
T* (If there is no response, the owner uses a tracking service such as Find My Device or Find My iPhone to) Tj
T* (locate the phone. Next, if the phone cannot be traced, the owner locks or erases the device remotely to) Tj
T* (protect personal data. Then, the owner changes the passwords of important accounts such as email,) Tj
T* (banking and social media. After that, the owner calls the service provider's helpline and blocks the SIM) Tj
T* (card. Next, the owner visits the nearest police station or the police online portal and files a complaint with) Tj
T* (the phone's details and IMEI number. Then, the police register the complaint and issue an) Tj
T* (acknowledgement copy. After that, the owner collects a duplicate SIM from the service provider by) Tj
T* (showing the complaint copy and an ID proof. Next, the owner blocks the phone's IMEI number on the) Tj
T* (CEIR portal using the complaint details. Finally, the owner notes the request ID so that the status can be) Tj
T* (tracked and the phone can be unblocked if it is recovered.) Tj
ET
BT
/F10 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.184 0.322 0.2 rg
56.6929133858267775 595.2758267716535556 Td
(3. Describe the process of organising a successful hackathon.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
70.8661417322834666 578.2679527559055259 Td
(First, the organisers decide the objective, theme and date of the hackathon. Next, they form committees) Tj
T* (for registration, technical support, logistics and publicity. Then, they prepare a budget and approach) Tj
T* (sponsors for funds and prizes. After that, they book the venue and arrange internet, power supply and) Tj
T* (refreshments. Next, they publicise the event on social media and open online registration for teams. Then,) Tj
T* (they shortlist the teams and share the problem statements and rules with them. After that, they invite) Tj
T* (mentors and judges and brief them about the evaluation criteria. On the day of the event, the teams build) Tj
T* (their prototypes while the mentors guide them. Then, each team presents its project to the judges, who) Tj
T* (evaluate it on innovation, feasibility and impact. Finally, the winners receive prizes and certificates, and) Tj
T* (the organisers collect feedback from the participants.) Tj
ET
BT
/F10 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.184 0.322 0.2 rg
56.6929133858267775 433.7010236220471597 Td
(4. Describe the process of applying for an internship.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
70.8661417322834666 416.69314960629913 Td
(First, the student identifies the field and the type of internship that match his or her interests and career) Tj
T* (goals. Next, the student prepares an updated resume that highlights skills, projects and achievements.) Tj
T* (Then, the student writes a short cover letter that explains why he or she is suited for the role. After that,) Tj
T* (the student creates or updates a profile on internship portals such as Internshala or LinkedIn. Next, the) Tj
T* (student searches for suitable openings and checks the eligibility, duration and stipend. Then, the student) Tj
T* (submits the application online along with the required documents. After that, the company shortlists the) Tj
T* (candidates and sends the interview or test details by email. Next, the student attends the interview or the) Tj
T* (screening test. If selected, the student receives an offer letter by email. Finally, the student accepts the) Tj
T* (offer and reports to the company on the joining date.) Tj
ET
BT
/F10 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.184 0.322 0.2 rg
56.6929133858267775 272.1262204724408775 Td
(5. Describe the process of applying for a PAN card.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
70.8661417322834666 255.1183464566928478 Td
(First, the applicant visits the official NSDL or UTIITSL website. Next, the applicant selects the online) Tj
T* (application for a new PAN card \(Form 49A for Indian citizens\). Then, the applicant chooses the category,) Tj
T* (such as individual, and fills in details like name, date of birth and address. After that, the applicant enters) Tj
T* (a mobile number and an email ID for communication. Next, the applicant uploads scanned copies of the) Tj
T* (proofs of identity, address and date of birth. Then, the applicant reviews all the details and corrects the) Tj
T* (errors, if any. After that, the applicant pays the application fee through net banking, card or UPI. Once the) Tj
T* (payment is successful, the system generates an acknowledgement number, which the applicant saves for) Tj
T* (tracking. Then, the Income Tax Department verifies the details and the documents. Finally, the PAN card) Tj
T* (is dispatched to the registered address by post, and an e-PAN is sent to the registered email.) Tj
ET
